    <briefdescription>
<para>Length-prefixed byte string passed between the <ref refid="namespace_m2" kindref="compound">M2</ref> front end and the engine. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="struct_m2__string__struct_a6fab19a0720d4857e68924fa5238efdd_1a6fab19a0720d4857e68924fa5238efdd" kindref="member">len</ref></computeroutput> is the byte count; <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_m2__string__struct_a65cd282ade4e5a7dc035e4f6897cccc0_1a65cd282ade4e5a7dc035e4f6897cccc0" kindref="member">array</ref></computeroutput> is a C99 flexible-array member that follows in the same allocation. Always handled as a pointer (<computeroutput>M2_string</computeroutput>), never as a value, so the trailing variable-length buffer travels with it. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
